# Timetable Proportion Restoration

## Changes Made
- Reverted the `minHeight` parameter of the table row cells (both vertical and horizontal views) back up to `100px` (from `76px`).
- This effectively gives the absolute-positioned event blocks enough vertical room to render as proper, comfortable "cards", eliminating the compressed or squashed badge-like look without breaking the correct horizontal span calculations. 
- Internal paddings (`p-1.5 md:px-2 md:py-1.5`) remain optimized so text flows nicely within the expanded card.

## Validation
- The frontend will auto-refresh. The timetable cells should look nicely padded and tall again, exactly as they did before the height reduction, but with the accurate NUSMods-style absolute width spanning.
